WEBVTT

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:03.600
As your Majesty has ordered,

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.850
I have recovered him.

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:06.740
Say, Ferris.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:11.970
This is the fourth day I've been working in here non-stop.

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:16.630
Any longer, and I think I'll die from some disaster in this mountain of documents.

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:19.370
What would you think of something like that?

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.100
Ryner!

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.070
Don't fall asleep, Ryner!

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:30.300
No, I'm tired now. Sorry, Ferris.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:33.260
No! Don't do it, Ryner!

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:36.680
Didn't we take a vow together, to get married after we made it off of the mountain?

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:41.240
Oh, is that how this story develops? Okay, I'll go with...

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:46.410
I-I wanted... to be happy... together with you...

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:48.470
R-Ryner!

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:50.610
Open your eyes!

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:53.880
Ryner, Ferris. Listen to me. There's a bit of trouble with...

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:55.700
Sion! This isn't the time!

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:59.250
Ryner just stopped breathing!

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:03.540
The causes were unexplained strong blows to the face, and overwork.

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:08.100
Can we move past that, Ryner? There's a job that needs handling right away...

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:12.860
I was nearly dead just now. I can't hear a thing anymore!

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:15.160
Please find someone else!

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:15.890
Nope.

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:18.170
He turned that down quick.

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:20.510
Please, Ryner.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:23.980
If these aren't handled within a week, there will be serious trouble.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:27.460
If this keeps up, there could be a birthday celebration.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:30.110
A birthday? Whose?

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:30.780
Mine.

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:32.240
Yours?

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:37.960
"Quiz Contest Concerning Torture and Punishment in the Roland Empire."

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:40.130
If we can spread understanding

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:45.370
of how harshly this nation punishes those who commit crimes,

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:48.340
it could lead to a reduction in of crime rates.

00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:51.140
I like it.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:55.050
But would this proposition be entertaining

00:03:55.050 --> 00:04:00.230
as an event at the king of Roland's birthday celebration?

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:03.650
Still, this year...

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:07.140
...I must ensure a successful celebration of our great king's day of birth!

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:14.350
Eight hundred and forty three, eight hundred and forty four... aw, crap!

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:18.680
My arm's starting to go out of control! I won't give in!

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:23.690
Yeesh. You're still recovering, and look at what a meathead you're being!

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:25.250
Who are you calling a meathead?!

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:29.170
If you keep pushing your limits, I'm telling Miss Noa!

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:32.550
Hey, that's not fair!

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:38.000
Wow, instant results! You and Miss Noa must be real close...

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:41.710
Then maybe I should tell Eslina everything?

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:45.510
About your thing with Lord Pearl's wife, or the thing with the widower Fazia?

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:49.700
Hey, hold on! It was just pleasantries, I wasn't going to do anything!

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:52.070
Pleasantries, huh?

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:53.450
That's right.

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:59.840
Your heads are both filled with spring colors, as always. It makes me envious.

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:01.500
Here comes the dark one.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:03.330
Are you making fun of us?

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:08.350
Not at all. It's a compliment. On that note, I wish to consult with you.

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:13.520
You two have succeeded in minimizing the content in your heads.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:15.470
I have just the job in mind for you both.

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:18.760
I'm gonna kill him, Calne.

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:20.220
All right, sir!

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:22.720
Goodness gracious.

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:24.640
I'm begging you, Ryner!

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:28.790
Beg all you want, you made me work all day yesterday and even more before that!

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:30.410
Damn it!

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:33.140
Fine then, you rest! Rest and get some sleep!

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:35.400
You haven't slept this whole time either, have you?!

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.340
Hold on, Ryner!

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:38.720
Go to sleep forever, right now!

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:01.480
Damn it. I'm not sticking around for more of that!

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:03.850
I'm going back to the inn and getting some sleep.

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:07.770
Ryner, what are you doing in a place like this?

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:12.540
That Sion just thinks way too seriously!

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:15.830
He should just sit back and celebrate his birthday.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:17.530
Y-Yeah, he should.

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:21.390
I know, right? Everyone said they wanted to celebrate it...

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:24.150
Birthday...? Birthday!

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:30.710
Oh, yeah... Sorry. I totally ditched your birthday party.

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:32.630
You remembered!

00:06:32.630 --> 00:06:35.460
Well, er... I'm really sorry.

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:41.390
It's okay! A lot happened after that, and I wasn't in much of a position to have a party.

00:06:41.390 --> 00:06:45.450
Just knowing that you remembered makes me happy, okay?

00:06:49.140 --> 00:06:53.460
Is it that late already? Sorry, Ryner. I'd better get back.

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:54.060
Sure.

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:56.010
See you, Ryner!

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:57.790
Get lots of rest!

00:06:57.790 --> 00:07:01.240
If you let that pretty-on-the-outside woman trick you into doing anything funny,

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:03.490
I'll never forgive you, okay?

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:05.920
Hey! Don't say weird stuff like that!

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:11.420
Truly, such a wonderful girl!

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:16.910
Even after having her birthday party canceled at the last minute,

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:18.550
Captain Milk behaves so gallantly!

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:21.840
Compared to that, some certain taboo breaker would be...

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:24.250
Trash, yes!

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:26.410
You're responsible for that to begin with!

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:27.430
Yes, of course!

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:31.940
That's why we were in the process of considering a means of atonement!

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:33.280
Atonement?

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:35.000
Yes, atonement.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.190
Right, atonement.

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:43.160
I see. Sion's birthday, huh?

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:48.320
Come to think of it, last year, he had a really dull celebration.

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:51.870
That's because Sion utterly despises luxury.

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:57.240
We must not allow such a dull ceremony to come to pass again this year.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:01.220
For the sake of Roland's future, I would like to borrow your strength, both of you.

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:05.720
All right! You can count on me, Gloomy!

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:08.670
Then, we'd better give it a little thought.

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.800
All right, it's meeting time!

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:13.070
We should hear the women's opinions, too.

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:15.150
Hey, yeah, good idea!

00:08:15.150 --> 00:08:17.300
That's something Gloomy would never think of.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:19.050
Let there be...

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:20.110
Ah, better not...

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:21.950
Better get Noa in on this!

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:23.860
Can I bring Eslina, too?

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:29.440
I don't think it's a bad idea, though...

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:31.370
The Torture and Assassination Festival.

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:34.690
We can build a stage in the plaza in front of the royal palace...

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:36.000
How about some stalls?

00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:40.220
We've got to give it more flair, more flash. Make it a festival.

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:42.460
How did they do that in Estabul?

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:47.540
Let's see. When they held festivals, they'd have a lot of fireworks.

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:48.530
Fireworks, huh?

00:08:48.530 --> 00:08:51.470
Those are the big things that get fired up into the sky, right?

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:52.890
Eslina?

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:59.140
I've never seen the really big ones! I'd love to see them just once.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:00.110
What do you think, sir?

00:09:00.110 --> 00:09:04.290
Why not? They'd add a lot of flair, and everyone could enjoy them.

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:07.430
That's true! Okay, let's make fireworks the main event.

00:09:07.430 --> 00:09:08.370
Really?!

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:10.210
One moment.

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:14.040
It takes quite a bit of time to prepare major fireworks.

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:16.460
The bigger ones can take half a year.

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:17.130
Half a year?!

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:19.720
If it has to be done in time to celebrate Lord Astal's birthday,

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:24.240
we couldn't do anything very spectacular if we just got started now.

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:26.860
I guess that wouldn't work, then.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:29.260
No, we're going to do fireworks.

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:30.950
Eh? But...

00:09:30.950 --> 00:09:33.600
I know just the guy for it.

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:43.220
Ryner. Don't you consider that attitude to be rude to the dumplings?

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:49.200
I'm at my limit, you know. I've got all kinds of trouble.

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:54.240
Ah, so a woman you tricked long ago demands punitive damages from you,

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:58.720
and to pay her off, you try to trick another woman so you can steal her money,

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:02.000
then your last moments are spent getting stabbed and dying in a ditch.

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:03.480
Do I have it about right?

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:05.810
Sure, whatever, we'll call it right.

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:07.830
But right now, it's dumpling time.

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:10.070
Forget all those troublesome things and focus on the dumplings.

00:10:10.070 --> 00:10:11.080
Right.

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:13.320
Well?

00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:15.220
Mm, delicious.

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:18.030
I've been made to eat dumplings from all over the place, thanks to you,

00:10:18.030 --> 00:10:20.190
but there's none that can compare to Wynnit.

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.190
Is that right?

00:10:23.410 --> 00:10:24.830
Is this a new recipe?

00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:27.650
It tastes different from usual, but it's pretty darn good.

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:29.230
What is it?

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:29.950
Nothing...

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:35.290
Oh, it looks like it's scored high marks with your partner! Good for you, little Ferris!

00:10:36.050 --> 00:10:36.870
Shop-keep!

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:41.330
That dumpling is a new recipe little Ferris came up with and made!

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:44.090
You made this?

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:46.300
Yeah.

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:50.510
Little Ferris dreams of running a dumpling shop of her own one day!

00:10:50.510 --> 00:10:51.340
A dumpling shop?!

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:54.010
You, huh?

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:56.950
Well, I guess you're always serious when it comes to dumplings.

00:10:56.950 --> 00:10:58.080
Of course I am!

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:02.140
Those who don't contend with dumplings seriously are punished by the god of dumplings!

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:03.860
What's this "Dumpling God" stuff?

00:11:03.860 --> 00:11:06.260
The Dumpling God is the god of dumplings.

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:10.450
He is the one absolute god who reigns over the world!

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:14.620
Hey! There he is, the man who naps for then thousand years!

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:15.700
Huh?!

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:19.710
Excuse us, there's a job we'd really like for you to do...

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:20.880
C'mon, let's go.

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:23.710
Hey! What are you doing?! Wait, let me go!

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:26.670
Get up and walk!

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:28.680
I can't walk the way you're holding me!

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:31.800
So your misdeeds are revealed, and the time has come for you to be thrown into the ditch.

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:33.720
Hey, wait!

00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:36.310
Let me go!

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:39.890
Stay in sound health, Ryner.

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:50.220
Can't you go any faster?

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:52.520
I can't! Any faster would be...

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:56.070
Damn. All the preparations were supposed to be in place!

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:06.020
Give it up.

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:08.820
There's no escape for you.

00:12:11.230 --> 00:12:13.890
Finally! Finally, this day has come!

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:17.520
Ever since that red-haired meathead dragged me into his idiotic plan,

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:19.120
I've been stuck working day and night!

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:23.230
So what's the big idea running off, you ass?! You jerk!

00:12:23.230 --> 00:12:24.270
Hurry it up!

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:27.810
Come on, men. Take him and go!

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:36.220
Hold on—

00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:40.430
Come on, you dogs, carry him!

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:42.730
I've got work to do! Area inspections...

00:12:42.730 --> 00:12:44.930
Bring him to the castle, put your back in it!

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:45.170
Yeah!

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:46.790
I'm counting on you!
Yeah!

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:47.200
One-two! One-two! One-two!

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:48.770
Move it!
One-two! One-two! One-two!

00:12:48.770 --> 00:12:50.350
One-two! One-two! One-two!

00:13:03.810 --> 00:13:06.890
Three cheers for Lord Sion!

00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:10.000
Brother Sion!

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:11.750
Your Majesty!

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:17.100
Your Majesty, everyone's waiting eagerly.

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:20.340
It's a bit sudden, but I would ask you to ignite the fireworks.

00:13:20.340 --> 00:13:21.380
Fireworks?

00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:23.220
We prepared them just for you.

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:26.340
But something this large-scale wasn't accounted for in the budget...

00:13:26.340 --> 00:13:27.430
Come on!

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:29.610
Look!

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:38.390
Everyone in this nation is celebrating for you.

00:13:38.390 --> 00:13:40.700
Please, answer their calls.

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:43.440
Thank you, everyone.

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:45.240
Please have a look at the mountains up ahead.

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:50.010
Fire an Izuchi in the direction of that small light.

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:51.420
Roger that.

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:55.410
What I seek is thunder.

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:57.450
Izuchi!

00:14:39.880 --> 00:14:41.120
Amazing!

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:42.740
Cool!

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:48.290
Here goes!

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:50.410
Happy birthday!

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:53.150
Thank you!

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:57.420
How's this? Looks delicious, doesn't it?

00:14:57.420 --> 00:14:59.760
"Happy Birthday."

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:01.650
Thank you! Huh?

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:03.130
Captain Milk.

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:05.420
Your attention, please!

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:07.120
Okay, here goes.

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:07.760
Five!

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:08.990
Four!

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:10.060
Three!

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:11.240
Two!

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:12.260
One!

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:53.470
Hm? Was that Sir Sion?

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:55.010
Sorry, I won't drink anymore.

00:16:00.880 --> 00:16:02.060
You're going?

00:16:14.350 --> 00:16:16.620
Your Majesty? Is something the matter?

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:19.880
I'd like to take the carriage out. Could you get it ready?

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:22.040
I'll call a coachman immediately.

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:23.890
No, I'll go alone.

00:16:23.890 --> 00:16:25.080
That would be...

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:26.750
I have someone to pick up.

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:29.130
Him.

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:33.800
I want to come for him.

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:58.370
Who would've expected it to start raining?

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:01.970
Ugh, cold! Better get back quick... Huh?

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:24.840
You're a lifesaver, Sion.

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:26.560
Thanks, Ryner.

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:28.580
Huh? For what?

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:32.480
The fireworks. You're the one who fired them off.

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:33.690
Yeah, sure.

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:36.970
The rain's started to get to me.

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:40.310
There's a place I'd like to stop off at, if you don't mind?

00:17:40.310 --> 00:17:42.030
I don't mind.

00:17:42.030 --> 00:17:43.880
All right, then.

00:17:49.390 --> 00:17:51.760
This is where you wanted to stop?

00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:54.360
This place sure brings back some memories.

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:58.000
Yes, it's the place where I first raised a toast with you.

00:17:58.720 --> 00:17:59.310
Ryner...

00:17:59.310 --> 00:18:00.800
Huh?

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:03.100
Thank you for today. I mean it.

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:06.920
Huh? Well, gotta be nice sometimes, I guess.

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:10.190
But after this, I'm gonna get one hell of a nap.

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:14.870
Not yet. Actually, there's still work left that needs to be done quickly.

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:19.810
Aw, cut it out. Any more of this, and I'd be dead for real.

00:18:20.610 --> 00:18:24.070
I guess working nonstop for over a tenday is pretty rough.

00:18:24.070 --> 00:18:29.770
You know, it'd have been nice if you'd realized that by the second day, or even the third day.

00:18:29.770 --> 00:18:33.290
I suppose so. Shall we get back and get some sleep, then?

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:36.510
Yeah! I'll head back to the inn.

00:18:37.060 --> 00:18:41.210
I'll send a carriage for you when you wake up, so we can pick up where we left off.

00:18:41.210 --> 00:18:42.600
No way.

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:44.940
I'll come for you in three hours.

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:48.810
Huh?! What the hell?! I've barely gotten any sleep!

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:51.500
Okay, how many hours should it wait?

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:52.560
How about three hundred hours?

00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:56.480
Okay. Then we'll meet in the middle and say four hours.

00:18:56.480 --> 00:19:00.430
How is that the middle?! Besides, you should get some sleep!

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:03.950
You probably haven't gotten any real sleep in ages! Right?

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:05.730
It can't be helped.

00:19:05.730 --> 00:19:08.050
To completely change this country,

00:19:08.050 --> 00:19:11.620
we still need widespread education, improved medical care,

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:15.820
tax reform, technological advancement, and, let's see...

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:20.050
Seriously, how much of a workaholic are you?

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:21.550
Oh, yeah, Sion.

00:19:37.670 --> 00:19:40.400
Sion... I'm sorry.

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:47.610
Back then, I thought the things you said were just empty dreams.

00:19:50.060 --> 00:19:54.010
"I'll become king of this land. I'll change everything.

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:58.250
I'll make the world you once desired."

00:20:02.670 --> 00:20:04.720
It wasn't an empty dream.

00:20:06.630 --> 00:20:10.100
This country has changed. You've changed it.

00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:12.560
To a world where everyone can live without crying.

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:16.050
A world where everyone can live with a smile.

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:21.650
It's an empty dream.

00:20:23.440 --> 00:20:27.070
How many friends have died for it?

00:20:27.070 --> 00:20:32.080
How many people do you think have died for the sake of my ideal?

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:35.620
How much was sacrificed for the world as it is now?

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:40.880
Even so, without you, this country would have remained dark forever.

00:20:41.610 --> 00:20:44.880
It's... enough.

00:20:48.240 --> 00:20:52.320
You're working plenty hard. I know that.

00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:56.400
So don't work yourself to the bone trying to punish yourself.

00:20:58.380 --> 00:21:00.440
This country has changed.

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:05.230
Even if you take it easy a little now, it won't go back to the way it was.

00:21:05.230 --> 00:21:09.620
There's no more need to be constantly afraid that what you're doing is wrong,

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:12.120
that you could be doing it better.

00:21:12.470 --> 00:21:14.860
Don't you have plenty of people now?

00:21:14.860 --> 00:21:19.010
Like that red-haired idiot, or the taboo breaker squadron guys.

00:21:19.010 --> 00:21:21.370
Or Ferris... or me.

00:21:21.370 --> 00:21:23.840
You don't have to bear everything by yourself anymore.

00:21:24.970 --> 00:21:27.840
This country is definitely changing, in a good way.

00:21:28.930 --> 00:21:30.270
Is it?

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:32.720
It is.

00:21:34.240 --> 00:21:37.550
If that was really true...

00:21:40.260 --> 00:21:42.110
...it would be so nice.

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:50.490
But it's all an empty dream.

00:23:21.470 --> 00:23:22.910
<i>For crying out loud!</i>

00:23:22.910 --> 00:23:25.680
<i>Why do things have to suck this much?!</i>

00:23:25.680 --> 00:23:28.980
<i>But, Sion, I said I wouldn't give up!</i>

00:23:28.980 --> 00:23:30.420
<i>So I'll give it all that I have!</i>

00:23:30.920 --> 00:23:34.880
<i>But this really, really, seriously sucks!</i>
